#
# TEMPLATE for knowledge/denylist.local — the client / person / project denylist the leak
# scanner checks the knowledge corpus against.
#
# Copy it:   cp knowledge/denylist.local.example knowledge/denylist.local
#
# knowledge/denylist.local is GITIGNORED and must stay that way. The denylist is itself a
# list of the client names we are protecting: shipping it would leak exactly what it
# exists to keep out. THIS file contains placeholders only and nothing else may be added
# to it, ever.
#
# A MISSING denylist.local is NOT a clean scan — `npm run leak:scan` and the bake both
# REFUSE when the file is absent, because "no denylist" and "the denylist found nothing"
# produce the same green tick and only one of them is safe.
#
# Format, one entry per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
#   acme-industries      a term — matched case-insensitively on a word boundary.
#                        Use one line per client name, per product name, per person.
#   project:ABC          a project key — matches the bare key and ABC-123 ticket keys.
#   /pattern/i           an explicit regex, for a name a word boundary will not catch
#                        (accented characters, an ampersand, a two-word brand).

# --- client and partner organisations -----------------------------------
placeholder-client-one
placeholder-client-two

# --- named people (colleagues, reviewers, requesters) -------------------
placeholder person-name

# --- client project keys ------------------------------------------------
project:PLACEHOLDERKEY

# --- anything a word boundary will not catch ----------------------------
# /placeholder\s*&\s*partners/i
